{"title":"Ezra","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Ezra"},"headingText":"Ezra","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\n::: {.book-summary}\n## Book Summary Insight\n\nEzra records the return from exile and the rebuilding of the Temple. The book emphasizes God's faithfulness in restoring His people through worship and obedience to His Word.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 1\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 1:3</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Who is among His people? Let him go up</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nReturn from exile begins\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter records Cyrus's decree allowing the Jews to return to Jerusalem. The key verse demonstrates God's sovereignty in moving rulers to fulfill His promises.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 2\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 2:64</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">The whole congregation together</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nSummary of returnees\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter lists those who returned from exile. The key verse emphasizes God's faithfulness in preserving a remnant for restoration.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 3\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 3:11</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">For He is good; His mercy endures forever</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nTemple rebuilding worship\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter describes the rebuilding of the altar and restoration of worship. The key verse highlights the priority of worship before reconstruction.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 4\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 4:4</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">The people weakened the hands of Judah</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nOpposition to the work\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter records opposition to rebuilding efforts. The key verse demonstrates that God's work often faces resistance from adversaries.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 5\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 5:5</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">The eye of their God was upon them</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nDivine protection\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter recounts the resumption of Temple construction through prophetic encouragement. The key verse emphasizes the power of God's word to renew obedience.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 6\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 6:14</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">They prospered through the prophesying</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nCompletion of the temple\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter records the completion and dedication of the Temple. The key verse celebrates God's faithfulness in bringing His work to completion.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 7\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 7:10</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Ezra prepared his heart to seek the Law</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nDefining verse of Ezra's ministry\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter introduces Ezra and his mission to Jerusalem. The key verse highlights Ezra's devotion to studying, obeying, and teaching God's law.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 8\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 8:23</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">We fasted and sought our God</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nDependence through prayer\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter records Ezra's journey and God's protection. The key verse demonstrates dependence upon God rather than human security.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 9\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 9:6</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">O my God, I am ashamed and blush to lift up my face</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nEzra's confession\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter recounts Ezra's grief over Israel's sin. The key verse emphasizes genuine repentance before a holy God.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 10\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 10:4</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Arise; for this matter belongs unto thee</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nCall to decisive action\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter records the people's response and covenant renewal. The key verse highlights repentance expressed through decisive obedience.\n:::\n\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n# Ezra\n\n::: {.book-summary}\n## Book Summary Insight\n\nEzra records the return from exile and the rebuilding of the Temple. The book emphasizes God's faithfulness in restoring His people through worship and obedience to His Word.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 1\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 1:3</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Who is among His people? Let him go up</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nReturn from exile begins\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter records Cyrus's decree allowing the Jews to return to Jerusalem. The key verse demonstrates God's sovereignty in moving rulers to fulfill His promises.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 2\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 2:64</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">The whole congregation together</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nSummary of returnees\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter lists those who returned from exile. The key verse emphasizes God's faithfulness in preserving a remnant for restoration.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 3\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 3:11</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">For He is good; His mercy endures forever</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nTemple rebuilding worship\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter describes the rebuilding of the altar and restoration of worship. The key verse highlights the priority of worship before reconstruction.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 4\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 4:4</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">The people weakened the hands of Judah</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nOpposition to the work\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter records opposition to rebuilding efforts. The key verse demonstrates that God's work often faces resistance from adversaries.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 5\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 5:5</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">The eye of their God was upon them</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nDivine protection\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter recounts the resumption of Temple construction through prophetic encouragement. The key verse emphasizes the power of God's word to renew obedience.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 6\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 6:14</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">They prospered through the prophesying</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nCompletion of the temple\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter records the completion and dedication of the Temple. The key verse celebrates God's faithfulness in bringing His work to completion.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 7\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 7:10</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Ezra prepared his heart to seek the Law</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nDefining verse of Ezra's ministry\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter introduces Ezra and his mission to Jerusalem. The key verse highlights Ezra's devotion to studying, obeying, and teaching God's law.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 8\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 8:23</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">We fasted and sought our God</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nDependence through prayer\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter records Ezra's journey and God's protection. The key verse demonstrates dependence upon God rather than human security.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 9\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 9:6</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">O my God, I am ashamed and blush to lift up my face</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nEzra's confession\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter recounts Ezra's grief over Israel's sin. The key verse emphasizes genuine repentance before a holy God.\n:::\n\n::: {.chapter-entry}\n## Chapter 10\n\n<div class=\"key-verse\">Ezra 10:4</div>\n\n<div class=\"identifier\">Arise; for this matter belongs unto thee</div>\n\n### Why This Verse\n\nCall to decisive action\n\n### Chapter Insight\n\nThis chapter records the people's response and covenant renewal. The key verse highlights repentance expressed through decisive obedience.\n:::\n\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":"auto","echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","css":["../../styles/bible.css"],"toc":true,"toc-depth":3,"number-sections":false,"output-file":"ezra.html"},"language":{"toc-title-document":"Table of contents","toc-title-website":"On this page","related-formats-title":"Other Formats","related-notebooks-title":"Notebooks","source-notebooks-prefix":"Source","other-links-title":"Other Links","code-links-title":"Code Links","launch-dev-container-title":"Launch Dev Container","launch-binder-title":"